        "subject": "feat(portal, console): one payment flow, receivers, app handoff by request id, two-person review",
        "body": "feat(portal, console): one payment flow, receivers, app handoff by request id, two-person review\n\nOwner, 2026-11-12 (not yet published):\n- \"Pay or renew\" is one compact card: the store(s) (one preselected; several for\n  a renewal), one action (renew, activate a waiting store, an employee seat at\n  one store), 1/3/12 months, the server's line items and total, then the manual\n  payment window. \"Add a store\" sits beside the stores (names checked as before,\n  each activity's price and the D158 replacement note kept). The page prices\n  nothing and never sends an amount.\n- The window offers only the service/number pairs the server lists (Bankily and\n  Sedad on 36 96 38 39 and 37 67 68 27), and sends the one chosen with the\n  payer's number and the screenshot; a proof still waiting is corrected there,\n  naming its revision. Nothing offered: said honestly, nothing can be sent.\n- \"My stores\": stores, status and requests, with a clear \"Pay or renew\"; the\n  request forms moved into the flow. The duplicate Help card is gone (the footer\n  has the links, with its own spacing again).\n- The activation link's request is read from the server by its id\n  (GET my-subscription/pending/:rid) and fills the flow; nothing about it\n  travels in the address. An employee seat requested in the app shows the\n  person's name; employees are still added and verified in the app.\n- Console review: where the customer says the money went; the first step opens\n  the access (\"verification pending\"); an opened proof offers only \"Deposit\n  found - confirm\" or Refuse, for a different administrator, with who opened it,\n  when, on which version, and the 24-hour target.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
